# Without the request budget on the context, a handler waiting on the database is
# never cancelled: the socket closes and the work goes on holding a connection.

title: the handler is mounted bare, so nothing bounds a request
file: cmd/pacioli/serve.go
run: go test -count=1 -run TestARequestPastItsBudgetIsRefusedOverASocket -v ./cmd/pacioli/
--- before
		Handler:           ledgerhttp.Deadline(d.request, h),
--- after
		Handler:           h,
